      "strategy": "capacity",
      "translation": "On Taumako Island in the Solomon Islands, women are the guardians of the land and sea. They harvest and process the pandanus tree (a small tree widely distributed in Polynesia, Micronesia, and other regions) to weave sails that power navigation\u2014a skill that has been passed down for over three thousand years. As islander Delsie Betty Bosi states, \u201cMen are responsible for building most of the indigenous leaders, and Hindou Oumarou Ibrahim, Chair of the 23rd Session of the United Nations Permanent Forum on Indigenous Issues, pointed out in April 2024, 'This knowledge is not theoretical but the crystallization of wisdom tested through centuries of practice.'\u201d"
