      "strategy": "capacity",
      "translation": "At dawn, the air is filled with a rusty humidity, mingling with the scent of charcoal smoke. The Paumari people are an indigenous group of about two thousand, residing on the vast lands of Amazonas in northwestern Brazil. Their self-definition cannot be found in scientific textbooks: \"We are the Water People, the only people truly living in the water.\" In 2009, the world's largest freshwater fish, the Arapaima, was reduced to only 266 adult fish, threatening the survival of the Paumari people."
