      "strategy": "capacity",
      "translation": "Another exciting application of quantum sensing in the medical field is the 'entangled camera,' which is currently being used for imaging breast cancer tissue samples. The scientific principle behind it sounds almost magical. This technology relies on the quantum entanglement of two types of light: one is infrared light, which is very suitable for biological imaging and can easily penetrate tissue; the other is visible light, which cannot penetrate tissue but can produce clearer images in the camera. This technology can provide us with relevant information about tissue samples detected by infrared light. The entangled camera can guide oncologists in quickly determining whether women should undergo chemotherapy after breast cancer surgery."
