      "strategy": "capacity",
      "translation": "However, bioprospecting has been criticized for \"free-riding,\" accused of exploiting the knowledge achievements of indigenous peoples and other local communities without compensation. When indigenous knowledge is not adequately recognized in scientific research, product development, or commercialization, and the users of this knowledge do not reasonably share benefits with the holders of traditional knowledge, this behavior can be termed \"biopiracy.\""
